You are tasked with creating a program that analyzes a given CSS file and extracts specific information about the CSS classes defined within it. Your program should be able to identify the classes and their associated properties, allowing for further analysis or manipulation of the CSS data.

Write a function or method `extractCSSInfo(css)` that takes a string `css` representing the contents of a CSS file as input. The function should parse the CSS content and return a dictionary mapping each CSS class to its properties.

For the purpose of this problem, a CSS class is defined as a block of CSS properties enclosed within curly braces `{}` and preceded by a period `.`. Each property is represented as a key-value pair within the class block.

Example:
Given the following CSS content:
```css
.sp-50 {
    width: 100%;
    height: 50px;
}

.sp-10 {
    width: 100%;
    height: 10px;
}

.el-shl-loading {
    background-image: url("shl-loading.gif");
}
```
The function call `extractCSSInfo(css)` should return the following dictionary:
```python
{
    "sp-50": {
        "width": "100%",
        "height": "50px"
    },
    "sp-10": {
        "width": "100%",
        "height": "10px"
    },
    "el-shl-loading": {
        "background-image": "url(\"shl-loading.gif\")"
    }
}
